From: junkyard
Subject: [PATCH] fingerprint/goodix: port to Linux 6.18 (lynx)

Port private/google-modules/fingerprint/goodix to the GrapheneOS Linux 6.18 GKI for the gs201 lynx build.
Mechanical API migrations, no intended behaviour change:

  - platform_driver.remove returns void (6.11)
  - devm_gpio_request() removed (6.18), use devm_gpio_request_one()

Files: gw9608/gf_spi.c, gw9608/platform.c

lynx-only (kernel/patches-lynx/): felix builds the 6.1 tree these
drivers were written for.

lynx-linus-mainline (android-mainline -> Linus' v7.3; ACK-only interfaces are
handled here rather than restored in the kernel, see kernel/patches/README.md):
  * Kbuild for the ddk_modules here, generated from BUILD.bazel by
    tools/bazel2kbuild.py, for the make-only build (kernel/kbuild.mk):
      fps_touch_handler/Kbuild
      gw9608/Kbuild
---
diff --git a/fps_touch_handler/Kbuild b/fps_touch_handler/Kbuild
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..5bd318b
--- /dev/null
+++ b/fps_touch_handler/Kbuild
@@ -0,0 +1,40 @@
